cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "A trained network, checked by Lean"
abstract: >-
  A two-layer neural network trained on half of the pairs of addition modulo 113, with Lean 4
  kernel-checked proofs that its frozen integer weights give the right answer on all 12,769
  inputs and that its circle (Fourier) waves alone suffice, plus an exact certificate built from
  that explanation.
authors:
  - family-names: Lince
    given-names: Thomas
repository-code: "https://github.com/teal-sea/lean-checked-network"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-10-15
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - neural networks
  - modular arithmetic
